WEBVTT

00:40.140 --> 00:47.860
Spice and Wolf

01:58.460 --> 02:00.330
A chronicler?

02:00.010 --> 02:04.010
<b>Episode 15
Bird Feather and Mysterious Ore</b>

02:00.330 --> 02:02.300
Yeah, is there one around here?

02:02.700 --> 02:05.730
Are you talking about the people who 
earn money from nobles and the Church

02:05.730 --> 02:07.940
by writing a diary about everything 
that happens in town?

02:07.940 --> 02:11.110
They aren't writing a diary. 
They're keeping historical records.

02:11.410 --> 02:13.090
What's the difference?

02:13.090 --> 02:18.240
They can earn a pretty penny just by sitting 
around all day and writing. How annoying.

02:18.240 --> 02:19.820
So? Know of any?

02:19.820 --> 02:21.450
Yeah, I know one.

02:21.450 --> 02:24.000
It's rumored that the chronicler 
is a runaway heretic

02:24.000 --> 02:25.830
that was kicked out of a convent somewhere.

02:25.830 --> 02:28.080
I just want to ask a few questions.

02:28.080 --> 02:31.170
I want to find old stories 
and legends from the North.

02:31.170 --> 02:33.980
You're interested in something peculiar again.

02:33.980 --> 02:39.060
Well, it'd be strange to suddenly show up 
on their doorstep. Do you know a middleman?

02:40.190 --> 02:42.570
Would someone from Rowen be best?

02:42.570 --> 02:43.260
Yeah.

02:43.260 --> 02:47.370
There's an old merchant 
named Gi Batos in the association.

02:47.370 --> 02:49.560
He's a fearless man.

02:49.560 --> 02:53.570
He does business with people 
no one should get involved with.

02:53.570 --> 02:56.980
I'm sure he has a good relationship 
with the chronicler.

02:56.980 --> 02:58.740
I'll connect you to him.

02:58.740 --> 02:59.770
That'd be great.

03:00.210 --> 03:03.950
Oh, and I'm planning to go to Nyohhira.

03:03.950 --> 03:07.120
I'd like to ask some Northerners about 
the route there and the situation there.

03:07.120 --> 03:10.720
Something like that's not a problem. 
I'll ask around for you.

03:10.720 --> 03:11.790
I owe you one.

03:13.080 --> 03:16.460
It's scary to think that's all it takes 
to get you to owe me one.

03:16.460 --> 03:18.600
Then, can I ask you for something else?

03:18.600 --> 03:20.880
Huh? What now?

03:21.140 --> 03:22.930
I want to buy some delicious bread.

03:22.930 --> 03:25.930
How about you introduce me 
to one of your best customers?

03:38.270 --> 03:41.090
Something smells good...

03:41.530 --> 03:43.130
How are you feeling?

03:43.850 --> 03:45.680
I am hungry...

03:45.680 --> 03:49.680
I thought as much. I went all out 
and bought some wheat bread.

03:56.490 --> 03:58.170
Are you not having any?

03:58.170 --> 03:59.230
I'm fine.

03:59.230 --> 04:00.710
I tested the taste earlier.

04:00.710 --> 04:02.100
Is that so?

04:06.310 --> 04:07.050
Hey.

04:08.220 --> 04:10.270
We can attend the festival now, can we not?

04:11.730 --> 04:13.800
Sorry. Not yet.

04:17.480 --> 04:20.230
Don't do that. Even if you're joking.

04:21.470 --> 04:24.450
I knew you were weak to things such as this!

04:24.450 --> 04:25.460
I shall remember.

04:25.460 --> 04:26.450
Hey, now.

04:26.450 --> 04:31.230
Hm, but why can't I go explore 
the town on my own?

04:31.230 --> 04:33.410
You'll go even if I say you can't.

04:34.250 --> 04:36.750
You're not wrong.

04:38.230 --> 04:39.500
Oh, that's right.

04:39.900 --> 04:42.420
I don't have any small change 
on me right now...

04:43.350 --> 04:45.050
Don't go crazy and spend it all.

04:49.280 --> 04:50.240
What's the matter?

04:51.670 --> 04:52.660
Well...

04:53.890 --> 04:57.640
I realize there is no point 
in going out alone, after all...

04:59.150 --> 05:01.390
What are you doing?

05:01.390 --> 05:02.000
Huh?

05:02.000 --> 05:06.330
If you take me along with you, 
I shall return this to you.

05:06.330 --> 05:08.960
Oh, well...

05:08.960 --> 05:10.280
I'm meeting with someone.

05:10.280 --> 05:13.410
If it is inconvenient for me 
to stay close, I will step away.

05:13.690 --> 05:15.790
So, will you take me with you?

05:17.150 --> 05:18.620
I'm really sorry...

05:19.110 --> 05:21.670
I might go somewhere else right after that.

05:22.150 --> 05:25.570
Even if I have you wait for me, 
it might be for the whole time.

05:25.570 --> 05:26.540
I see.

05:27.360 --> 05:29.110
Everything should be taken care of by tomorrow.

05:29.660 --> 05:32.680
Can you endure and be alone for today?

05:35.110 --> 05:38.310
Well, it is not very good to get in your way.

05:38.990 --> 05:41.570
Then, I shall wander around on my own.

05:41.930 --> 05:42.930
Sorry...

05:42.930 --> 05:48.030
Oh, right. If I bring someone back with me, 
please be considerate and leave the room.

05:50.840 --> 05:53.130
Now that I have seen such a cute expression,

05:53.130 --> 05:55.700
I should be able to spend 
the rest of the day alone!

05:56.010 --> 05:57.120
Hey, now...

05:57.120 --> 06:03.300
Well, for now, snuggling in your arms 
is the best. Do not fret...

06:08.300 --> 06:12.550
<i>The town that worshiped a pagan wolf god...</i>

06:12.980 --> 06:18.760
The town of Yoitsu was annihilated 
by a monstrous bear!

06:21.050 --> 06:22.740
It might not be true...

06:29.610 --> 06:31.950
Oh, you'll be able to recognize him right away.

06:31.950 --> 06:34.780
He's a large man that looks like 
a coffin crushed vertically...

06:34.780 --> 06:35.840
Mr. Lawrence?

06:40.380 --> 06:42.420
Thank you for finding us a place to stay.

06:43.060 --> 06:48.380
Not at all! Thank you for 
eating a lot of fish dishes there.

06:48.380 --> 06:51.160
My picky companion 
spoke very highly of the food there.

06:51.160 --> 06:53.090
She says you have a good eye for fish.

06:53.090 --> 06:55.620
I am happy to hear that!

06:55.620 --> 06:58.730
I will look for other things for her to enjoy.

07:02.020 --> 07:05.860
By the way, Mr. Lawrence, 
are you busy after this?

07:06.190 --> 07:10.300
I need to meet with Mr. Batos 
and ask him a few things.

07:10.300 --> 07:12.030
I see...

07:12.030 --> 07:13.280
What's the matter?

07:13.280 --> 07:18.450
Well, I wanted to show you around town.

07:18.450 --> 07:19.560
Show me around?

07:19.560 --> 07:23.660
Yes, divine providence 
must have brought us together.

07:23.660 --> 07:28.630
I thought I could broaden my view if
I talked with a traveling merchant like you...

07:29.970 --> 07:31.840
Come to think of it, my companion Holo

07:31.840 --> 07:34.800
has also been begging me to explore 
the town with her this morning.

07:34.800 --> 07:38.590
If you don't mind, I would love 
to show Ms. Holo around at least!

07:38.590 --> 07:40.540
No, I don't want to ask you for too much...

07:40.540 --> 07:43.810
Actually, I've already finished 
my work for today and I'm free.

07:44.100 --> 07:47.020
If I loiter around alone, all my profits 
will just go towards some alcohol.

07:47.020 --> 07:48.820
Please allow me to show her around!

07:49.180 --> 07:50.440
Is that so?

07:50.440 --> 07:55.280
However, she's not the type to quietly 
stay at the inn just because I ask her to.

07:55.280 --> 07:56.810
She might already be out...

07:57.530 --> 08:00.920
I've been meaning to ask the inn 
about some purchases,

08:00.920 --> 08:03.660
so I can stop by and invite her 
if she happens to be there!

08:03.660 --> 08:04.720
Thank you very much.

08:04.720 --> 08:05.710
Not at all!

08:06.200 --> 08:09.040
Please let me show you 
around next time, Mr. Lawrence.

08:11.620 --> 08:13.670
Are you Mr. Kraft Lawrence?

08:14.550 --> 08:15.790
You're...

08:15.790 --> 08:17.270
I'm Gi Batos.

08:19.740 --> 08:25.530
I heard you were looking for a chronicler 
to ask about old stories of the north.

08:25.530 --> 08:27.230
Yes, that's right.

08:27.230 --> 08:32.990
Well, you're a strange one. Are you looking 
for some kind of inspiration to make money?

08:32.990 --> 08:35.790
No, that's not the reason.

08:35.790 --> 08:37.620
Perhaps you could call it a whim?

08:37.620 --> 08:39.050
I see.

08:39.050 --> 08:41.880
What an interesting hobby for someone so young.

08:42.860 --> 08:47.000
I've only recently 
grown interested in old stories.

08:47.300 --> 08:51.970
After doing business in the same area for 
decades, I suddenly realized something.

08:51.970 --> 08:55.720
The world I know is actually very small.

08:55.720 --> 08:57.840
Even so, even here,

08:57.840 --> 09:04.450
I know nothing about the people who have 
been coming and going for hundreds of years.

09:05.400 --> 09:08.690
That's why I wanted to know 
about a world that I haven't seen.

09:08.690 --> 09:13.110
Even if they're legends, I want to know
about the stories of a past that

09:13.110 --> 09:16.440
I can never experience due to God's fickleness.

09:17.900 --> 09:19.780
I understand a little how you feel.

09:19.780 --> 09:24.160
I was busy chasing 
after profits when I was young.

09:24.160 --> 09:28.450
My life might have been completely 
different if I had taken a moment

09:28.450 --> 09:31.250
to make time for such things.

09:31.670 --> 09:35.500
I'm a little envious of you, Mr. Lawrence, 
for your interest at such a young age...

09:35.500 --> 09:37.340
It's just a whim.

09:38.470 --> 09:41.010
Um, the person living here...

09:41.320 --> 09:45.520
Yes, this is the living quarters 
of those chased by the Church.

09:46.360 --> 09:48.150
An alchemist...

09:48.450 --> 09:51.870
Yes. Though they aren't 
considered criminals here,

09:51.870 --> 09:55.850
they'd be hanged the moment they set 
foot near places like Ruvinheigen.

09:55.850 --> 09:58.110
Be that as it may,

09:58.920 --> 10:01.760
the people here are all good people.

10:15.030 --> 10:16.630
Is this the smell of sulfur?

10:16.630 --> 10:19.860
Oh? You even dabble in medicine?

10:19.860 --> 10:22.860
No, I just know a little about it.

10:23.790 --> 10:26.190
Knowledge is a merchant's weapon.

10:26.190 --> 10:27.310
You flatter me.

10:28.380 --> 10:30.450
There are a lot of birds.

10:30.450 --> 10:33.940
Not all poisonous winds smell bad.

10:33.940 --> 10:36.940
We have to be wary if a bird suddenly dies.

10:38.860 --> 10:43.330
Mr. Batos, is it very profitable doing 
business with alchemists?

10:43.330 --> 10:46.200
I feel like there are a lot of risks 
to working with them...

10:46.200 --> 10:48.830
Not only do they buy 
a lot of gold, silver, and copper...

10:48.830 --> 10:54.610
They also purchase iron, lead, tin, 
mercury, sulfur, and phosphorous.

10:54.610 --> 10:58.590
Iron and lead? The items are 
more normal than I expected.

11:00.520 --> 11:04.430
Many people think that 
alchemists dabble in magic,

11:04.430 --> 11:07.600
but they aren't much different from goldsmiths.

11:07.600 --> 11:08.270
Although...

11:08.540 --> 11:12.430
Some of them <i>do</i> research magic.

11:13.650 --> 11:18.270
However, I've only heard rumors 
and never met such alchemists.

11:18.270 --> 11:20.280
I-Is that so...

11:21.730 --> 11:25.820
There's no need to be so nervous. 
They're all good people.

11:25.820 --> 11:27.020
Y-Yes...

11:31.240 --> 11:32.540
Excuse us!

11:40.800 --> 11:43.050
Oh, Mr. Batos...

11:43.420 --> 11:46.640
Long time no see. 
Looks like you've been doing well.

11:46.640 --> 11:49.100
Right back at you.

11:49.100 --> 11:52.160
I can't believe you walked around 
the mountains of Hyoram unscathed.

11:52.160 --> 11:54.770
God must love you very much.

11:55.150 --> 11:57.210
Oh, what a handsome man.

11:57.210 --> 12:00.650
But your expression tells me 
that you think I'm a witch.

12:00.650 --> 12:02.530
N-No, that's...

12:02.530 --> 12:05.950
Madam, this is a traveling merchant...

12:05.950 --> 12:07.920
My name is Kraft Lawrence.

12:08.490 --> 12:13.210
Is Dian Rubens currently home? 
May I speak with him?

12:14.580 --> 12:17.250
Oh, you didn't tell him, Mr. Batos?

12:17.250 --> 12:18.150
Oh...

12:18.930 --> 12:20.750
I am Dian Rubens.

12:20.750 --> 12:21.300
Huh?!

12:21.620 --> 12:26.050
It sounds like a man's name, doesn't it? 
Please feel free to call me Diana.

12:33.060 --> 12:36.560
First, I apologize for the sudden visit.

12:36.560 --> 12:39.150
No, please don't worry about that...

12:39.480 --> 12:40.840
Actually, Ms. Rubens...

12:40.840 --> 12:41.980
Diana.

12:42.710 --> 12:43.490
Excuse me...

12:44.850 --> 12:46.240
Actually, Ms. Diana,

12:46.500 --> 12:50.040
I wanted to ask about various 
old stories from the northern lands...

12:50.040 --> 12:51.220
The north?

12:51.220 --> 12:51.950
Yes.

12:52.710 --> 12:55.460
I was sure you were going to 
talk about a business deal...

12:55.460 --> 12:57.180
Please don't joke.

12:57.180 --> 13:00.090
You would have shown him the door 
if he came to talk business, wouldn't you?

13:01.590 --> 13:05.340
However, I don't know if the stories 
I know will satisfy you...

13:05.660 --> 13:10.630
I want to hear old stories 
about a town called Yoitsu.

13:11.050 --> 13:13.060
Oh, Yoitsu...

13:13.060 --> 13:17.440
The town that was destroyed 
by a bear that hunts the moon...

13:21.990 --> 13:23.940
The Moon-Hunting Bear.

13:24.370 --> 13:28.780
I believed it's pronounced 
<i>Irawa Will Mhedhend</i>.

13:29.230 --> 13:34.350
It is quite an old story, but there are 
many legends about that bear.

13:34.350 --> 13:38.170
I'm not interested in the bear, 
but about the town called Yoitsu.

13:38.170 --> 13:39.630
The town?

13:39.630 --> 13:40.560
Yes.

13:40.560 --> 13:43.880
For certain reasons, I am looking 
for the location of Yoitsu.

13:43.880 --> 13:45.440
The location?

13:46.900 --> 13:50.050
Location... Location...

13:50.050 --> 13:51.300
Do you not know?

13:56.440 --> 13:57.720
I remember.

13:58.380 --> 14:04.480
At the source of the Rohm River that runs 
north from Proania is a town called Lenos...

14:04.480 --> 14:07.990
If I remember correctly, it's a town 
known for their lumber and fur.

14:07.990 --> 14:10.740
It'll be easier to explain 
if you know the town.

14:10.740 --> 14:13.370
There is an old story 
passed down from that town.

14:14.990 --> 14:19.830
Long ago, a lone wolf appeared in the village.

14:19.830 --> 14:22.460
She called herself Holou of Yoitsu.

14:22.460 --> 14:25.620
Her frame was so tall 
we could only crane our necks upwards.

14:26.400 --> 14:29.160
Though we thought she came 
to bring divine punishment,

14:29.160 --> 14:32.760
Holou told us she came from 
the deep mountain forests of the east

14:32.760 --> 14:35.660
to travel southward.

14:36.120 --> 14:40.010
The wolf loved wine and would sometimes 
transform into a young girl

14:40.010 --> 14:42.440
to dance with the village girls.

14:42.440 --> 14:48.820
Her form looked younger than her age, yet, 
she had a tail unlike those of humankind.

14:48.820 --> 14:55.500
After some time, she promised 
good harvests and continued southward.

14:55.500 --> 14:57.830
Starting that year,

14:57.830 --> 15:02.180
our harvests grew rich and thus 
we call her Wheat-Tailed Holou...

15:03.990 --> 15:05.250
Is that of any help?

15:08.430 --> 15:09.620
Yes!

15:09.620 --> 15:12.870
There are only so many 
mountains east of Lenos.

15:12.870 --> 15:14.260
I couldn't ask for a better clue.

15:15.380 --> 15:16.880
That's good to hear.

15:17.180 --> 15:19.610
I would like to show my thanks to you...

15:20.190 --> 15:24.140
As you can see, even though I am 
currently on the run from the Church,

15:24.140 --> 15:27.120
I love old stories from pagan lands.

15:27.620 --> 15:32.820
Old stories and legends that 
haven't been twisted by the Church...

15:33.120 --> 15:37.310
Haven't you come across such a story or two?

15:39.290 --> 15:40.430
I understand...

15:42.730 --> 15:45.380
Then, let me tell you a special one.

15:46.830 --> 15:49.330
In a certain village 
filled with vast fields of wheat,

15:49.330 --> 15:53.350
a wolf is worshiped 
as the bringer of harvests...

15:56.810 --> 16:01.640
It's been a while since I've talked about 
legendary dragons and cities of gold.

16:01.640 --> 16:05.490
There was a time when I also 
dreamt of traveling as a knight

16:05.490 --> 16:07.070
with a single sword at my hip.

16:07.390 --> 16:09.150
Thank you for your help today.

16:09.150 --> 16:10.630
Not at all.

16:10.630 --> 16:15.660
I'm happy, since a lot of people 
nag when I visit the madam alone.

16:15.660 --> 16:18.990
On top of that, I was able to 
hear a very interesting story.

16:18.990 --> 16:20.500
Please ask me for this kind of thing anytime.

16:20.500 --> 16:22.370
Yes! Gladly!

16:25.800 --> 16:28.290
Oh, Mr. Lawrence.

16:28.290 --> 16:29.840
Long time no see.

16:30.130 --> 16:31.770
It has been a long time.

16:31.770 --> 16:33.640
Oh! Playboy!

16:35.410 --> 16:36.670
Well, have a drink.

16:36.670 --> 16:40.650
Yeah, so about the information 
I asked for this morning...

16:41.350 --> 16:42.980
Hey! That's too much!

16:43.550 --> 16:44.980
Goodness...

16:44.980 --> 16:47.020
So? What about it?

16:48.360 --> 16:49.850
Well, I've changed destinations.

16:49.850 --> 16:51.230
You know the town of Lenos?

16:51.230 --> 16:52.360
What?

16:52.360 --> 16:55.360
I already gathered 
some information about Nyohhira...

16:55.360 --> 16:57.870
Sorry, the situation has changed.

16:57.870 --> 17:02.030
So, is it true that you're currently 
in a fight with your companion?

17:02.030 --> 17:02.830
What'd you say?!

17:04.340 --> 17:06.380
I've already looked into you, playboy!

17:06.380 --> 17:11.210
It's well-known in these parts that you're 
staying in a nice inn with a gorgeous nun.

17:11.490 --> 17:14.760
Now I know what 
"fearless before God" truly means.

17:14.760 --> 17:17.050
My companion and I aren't in 
a relationship that's juicy enough

17:17.050 --> 17:18.410
to talk about over drinks.

17:18.410 --> 17:20.140
But why do you think we're fighting?

17:20.140 --> 17:21.720
Just a little bit ago,

17:21.720 --> 17:24.290
rumors that your companion and 
a young merchant from our association

17:24.290 --> 17:27.380
were walking around started coming in.

17:27.380 --> 17:30.510
Oh, you're talking about Mr. Amati.

17:30.510 --> 17:33.420
Oh, you've already given up?

17:34.440 --> 17:36.280
Unfortunately, you have the wrong idea.

17:37.000 --> 17:40.920
I've been busy all day and couldn't 
accompany my companion.

17:40.920 --> 17:45.790
Mr. Amati was free, so he offered 
to show her around town. That's all.

17:47.470 --> 17:48.420
Unsatisfied?

17:48.420 --> 17:52.120
Let me warn you as a fellow merchant.

17:52.120 --> 17:54.670
Don't underestimate Amati.

17:54.670 --> 17:58.990
Do you know how much fish he
deals with at such a young age?

17:58.990 --> 18:01.810
I know. I saw it myself.

18:02.540 --> 18:04.320
But there's nothing to worry about.

18:04.320 --> 18:06.680
My companion isn't such a frivolous person.

18:06.940 --> 18:09.080
That's a lot of confidence!

18:09.080 --> 18:13.140
If I found out Adele was 
walking around with Amati,

18:13.140 --> 18:15.820
I'd give up immediately 
because I wouldn't stand a chance.

18:15.820 --> 18:18.110
What about me and Mr. Amati?!

18:19.400 --> 18:21.280
I was talking about 
how I'd burn up with jealousy

18:21.280 --> 18:25.580
if that happened, 
because of how much I love you!

18:25.920 --> 18:28.250
Just burn up with jealousy then.

18:28.250 --> 18:32.200
I'll use that fire to bake 
Mr. Amati a delicious pie.

18:32.200 --> 18:33.210
A-Adele...

18:33.210 --> 18:35.960
I'm sorry! I'll help close up the shop!

18:45.350 --> 18:47.840
I cannot breathe...

18:48.300 --> 18:50.020
That scarf!

18:50.020 --> 18:52.400
Hey...

18:52.750 --> 18:55.070
Come and help me...

19:00.750 --> 19:02.980
How much did you drink and eat?

19:07.890 --> 19:10.460
You even had him buy such 
an expensive looking thing.

19:10.460 --> 19:12.580
I shall sleep...

19:12.830 --> 19:15.710
Hey, what else did you have him buy?

19:23.250 --> 19:24.410
This is...

19:28.520 --> 19:31.090
It is very high-quality fur.

19:31.090 --> 19:33.400
Though it is still lacking compared to my tail.

19:33.400 --> 19:38.430
You can't accept such nice things 
and not give anything back...

19:39.010 --> 19:40.370
Goodness.

19:40.370 --> 19:43.910
Getting in your good graces 
drags a man into the red.

19:44.870 --> 19:47.040
Did he ask you about our relationship?

19:47.860 --> 19:51.330
I am more interested in why 
you would ask about such a thing...

19:51.330 --> 19:54.630
It won't be good if our stories don't match.

19:56.100 --> 19:57.350
Well, fine.

19:57.940 --> 20:01.840
I told him that I am a traveling nun 
that you saved from bad people

20:01.840 --> 20:04.840
who were trying to sell me off.

20:05.550 --> 20:10.480
And, after being saved by you, 
I was shouldered with a huge debt.

20:10.480 --> 20:13.610
The debt is so enormous I could 
never pay it back, so I am currently

20:13.610 --> 20:16.440
paying you back by praying 
for your safety during our travels.

20:16.440 --> 20:19.870
Ah, how pitiful I am...

20:19.870 --> 20:21.650
I spoke of it quite sadly.

20:23.210 --> 20:25.980
That totally makes me sound like a villain...

20:25.980 --> 20:27.160
And? What's this?

20:27.160 --> 20:28.370
Oh, that?

20:28.370 --> 20:30.600
A fortune teller was using it!

20:30.600 --> 20:33.160
I was told it was a die 
that could see through fate!

20:33.160 --> 20:35.080
Does it not have an excellent shape?

20:35.080 --> 20:38.210
I am impressed with such craftsmanship.

20:38.210 --> 20:40.340
I am sure it can be sold for a high price!

20:40.620 --> 20:41.670
Fool.

20:42.520 --> 20:44.500
Do you really think 
something like this can be sold?

20:44.500 --> 20:45.430
What?!

20:45.430 --> 20:48.810
This is a natural mineral called pyrite.

20:48.810 --> 20:51.400
It naturally chips off 
in this shape when it's mined.

20:51.400 --> 20:52.600
Impossible.

20:52.600 --> 20:55.100
I'm not lying. You can tell, can't you?

20:56.850 --> 21:01.500
It's usually given as gift or used to 
con others into thinking it's gold.

21:01.500 --> 21:03.860
There weren't a lot of people 
buying it, were there?

21:03.860 --> 21:04.860
There were a lot of people.

21:04.860 --> 21:06.410
Huh? Really?!

21:06.410 --> 21:07.370
Yes.

21:09.030 --> 21:14.080
The fortune teller said that anyone 
could predict their fate with these dice...

21:14.080 --> 21:19.090
There were many who wanted to buy some 
to heal sicknesses and ward away evil.

21:19.090 --> 21:21.130
And you believed it?!

21:21.670 --> 21:26.690
The fortune teller was quite skilled 
and I was very impressed...

21:26.690 --> 21:29.010
Amati was able to 
successfully bid for this die.

21:29.010 --> 21:31.350
An auction? That's how popular it was?!

21:31.350 --> 21:33.940
Everyone grew quite excited.

21:33.940 --> 21:36.940
It was the first time I witnessed 
an auction, and it was amazing.

21:37.670 --> 21:40.200
They took advantage 
of the festive atmosphere...

21:40.200 --> 21:42.400
What a clever business strategy.

21:51.320 --> 21:53.480
I apologize for coming so early in the morning!

21:53.480 --> 21:56.660
I have a message from my... master...

22:00.650 --> 22:02.610
So? What's the message?

22:02.610 --> 22:03.210
Oh...

22:03.480 --> 22:05.580
Y-Yes! Actually...

22:08.340 --> 22:09.890
Mr. Lawrence!

23:45.060 --> 23:50.070
Episode 16

23:45.060 --> 23:50.070
Night of the Festival and Misaligned Gear

23:45.890 --> 23:49.690
